WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.910
A container ship pulls out of port,
stacked high with steel boxes.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.610
Its engines burn more fuel than a lorry's:

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.250
huge amounts of it.

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.450
Yet it may be the cleanest
way to move goods.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.790
How can that be?

6
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.390
Is it the sea air, cleaning the exhaust?

7
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.390
The wind?

8
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.650
Better engines?

9
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.550
In this mission, you'll learn
how to compare transport fairly,

10
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.500
by sea, by air and by land.

11
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.130
Then you'll weigh each
mode on environmental,

12
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.730
economic and social grounds, from cut
flowers to transport emissions in Northern

13
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.890
Ireland.

14
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.530
Your mission: find out how a fuel-hungry
ship could be the cleanest way to move

15
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.310
goods.
